    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "True misses (hits=0, not degraded)",
      "description": "Each row is one query that found nothing although every retrieval stage worked. Read: 'query' = what was asked, 'filters' = metadata filters applied (a wrong filter is the most common cause), project/agent_id/user_id = scope. lexical/semantic/rerank = candidates found per stage (0 everywhere = nothing relevant stored; empty = stage did not run). Action: search the CMS for the expected memory under the same user/agent; if it exists, compare scopes/filters; if not, it was never stored. candidates (only /query events) = results before the score threshold: candidates > 0 means something was found but filtered out by min_score_memory, so lower the threshold or reword; candidates = 0 (or empty on search/retrieve) means nothing matched at all.",
